8kloud-switcher (0.7.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Add an SRT STREAM card to the console's OUTPUTS tab. It edits the
    transport (send on/off, listener/caller/rendezvous, host, port, latency
    in ms, passphrase and AES key length, stream id, any other FFmpeg srt
    option) and the encoding (HEVC/AV1, video and AAC bitrates, keyframe
    interval, NVENC preset and path). The fields fold into the one FFmpeg
    URL the show file stores and --srt-out takes, so existing show files
    keep working and a pasted URL fills the fields; SEND off parks the URL.
  * The encoder backend and preset, CLI-only until now, persist in the
    show file. New --srt-keyframe SEC and --srt-audio-bitrate KBPS flags on
    both executables; both NVENC backends take the keyframe interval.

 -- Devin Block <devin@devinblock.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 02:02:16 +0000

